1. The function returns an empty string, as specified in your prompt.
2. The function supports both inline and external scripts by creating script tags for inline scripts and enqueuing external scripts to load concurrently.
3. External scripts are loaded in parallel up to the configurable limit (`MAX_EXTERNAL_SCRIPTS`).
4. A queue is used to manage loading of external scripts, ensuring that only a limited number are requested at once.
5. The function implements a timeout mechanism to prevent script loading from blocking the main thread for too long (`SCRIPT_LOAD_TIMEOUT`).
6. In case an external script fails to load, it logs an error and continues loading other scripts without blocking the page.
7. If all external scripts fail to load, inline scripts are executed after the timeout to ensure they are loaded last.

